description:
The final project reads commands like `add 2026-03-14 09:00 90 Team meeting`. Parse a line into a sealed command type, so the rest of the program can `switch` over it:

```java
// Command.java
sealed interface Command {
    record Add(LocalDateTime start, int minutes, String title) implements Command { }
    record Remove(String title) implements Command { }
    record Day(LocalDate date) implements Command { }
    record Free(LocalDate date, int minutes) implements Command { }
    record Summary() implements Command { }
    record Quit() implements Command { }
    record Invalid(String message) implements Command { }

    static Command parse(String line)
}
```

| Input | Result |
|---|---|
| `add <yyyy-MM-dd> <HH:mm> <minutes> <title...>` | `Add`; the title is the rest of the line, words joined by single spaces |
| `remove <title...>` | `Remove` |
| `day <yyyy-MM-dd>` | `Day` |
| `free <yyyy-MM-dd> <minutes>` | `Free` |
| `summary`, `quit` | `Summary`, `Quit` |

The command word ignores case and extra spaces. Problems give `Invalid` with one of these messages:
- `Usage: add <date> <time> <minutes> <title>` (and likewise `Usage: remove <title>`, `Usage: day <date>`, `Usage: free <date> <minutes>`) for missing or extra arguments; `summary` and `quit` ignore extra words;
- `Bad date or time` when a date or time does not parse (strict `yyyy-MM-dd` and `HH:mm`, so `2026-02-30` is bad);
- `Minutes must be between 5 and 720` for a number outside that range, and `Bad number` for text that is not a whole number;
- `Unknown command: <word>` for anything else, and `Empty line` for a blank line.

